    {
      "doc_type": "data_dictionary",
      "year": 2008,
      "title": "Banner Data Standards Manual",
      "url": "https://www.aamu.edu/about/administrative-offices/information-technology-services/support/banner-information/_documents/data-standards-manual.pdf",
      "summary": "The Data Standards Manual, approved by the Banner Data Standards Committee, establishes guidelines for the stewardship and integrity of Alabama A&M University's data within the Banner database. Initially published in 2008 and revised in 2010, it covers topics such as data confidentiality, access, maintenance, and use across various university departments. The manual aims to ensure the accuracy, security, and proper access to data while complying with federal regulations like FERPA and HIPAA. It includes comprehensive standards for handling 'Person' and 'Non-Person' data, addressing everything from name, address, and phone number formats to the procedures for modifying records. The manual supports the university's implementation of the SunGard Higher Education Banner ERP System, facilitating integrated administrative functions and information sharing across campus.",
